WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:06.040
In "Andor," the planet Ferrix is a hotbed
of activity leading up to Maarva Andor's funeral.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:10.880
Imperial forces land on the planet as rebel
agents huddle, and the whole town is abuzz

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.340
with preparations.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.140
In a shot of a local bar early in Episode
12, a smaller patron is seen walking back

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:19.280
to a table where their drink is waiting.

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:24.119
It's dark in the bar, and the shot only lasts
for a couple of seconds, but the alien appears

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:26.670
to be the same species as Maz Kanata.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:31.900
The bar-goer has the same stature, head shape,
and even similar goggles to Maz, making this

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.030
seem like an intentional Easter egg.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.040
"Andor" already has a vaguely similar alien
in the doctor who tries to save Nemik in Episode

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.879
6, but that character is pretty clearly a
different species.

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:48.000
The alien on Ferrix, on the other hand, looks
to be exactly the same kind of creature as Maz.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.379
Of course, since we still don't know the name
or history of that species, this little cameo

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:54.219
remains shrouded in mystery.

